  "verbalization": "Fenofibrate is implicated in the interaction with NCI-H446 through a series of target relationships, primarily through HepG2 cells. The evidence suggests that fenofibrate acts as a target for HepG2, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including S-Methylmethionine Sufonium, Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, and Glycitein. These compounds all ultimately target NCI-H446, indicating a potential pathway where fenofibrate may influence NCI-H446 through these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where fenofibrate could modulate the activity of these compounds, thereby affecting NCI-H446. The evidence supports a role for fenofibrate in the regulation of NCI-H446 through a network of targets, emphasizing the importance of HepG2 as a central node in this relationship.",
